WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.450
London, 1854.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.120
Cholera deaths cluster
around one public water pump.

3
00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.290
John Snow maps the deaths.

4
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.030
The pump handle is removed,
and the outbreak dies away.

5
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.380
Nobody at the time knew
that a microbe was to blame.

6
00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:18.070
Yet your body carries
trillions of microbes,

7
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.730
and very few of them ever make you ill.

8
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:25.270
So what makes one microbe a pathogen,
while its neighbours do you no harm?

9
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.390
In this mission, you'll meet
the main groups of microbes,

10
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.610
and the many that live on you quietly.

11
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.400
Then you'll learn what
makes a disease infectious,

12
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.180
able to pass from one host to the next.

13
00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.710
Your mission: find out what
makes something a pathogen.
